+### Duration
+
+{class}`Duration` converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of
+seconds, such as `120`, or one or more number and unit pairs, such as `1h30m`. The units are `d` (days), `h` (hours),
+`m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear at most once and they must be in that order. Units are
+case-insensitive. Spaces, signs, and decimals are not allowed.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
